# Controls

Pick the control from how many options there are. A dropdown is the last resort.

| Situation | Use |
|---|---|
| Two exclusive states | Switch or toggle |
| Under about 5 exclusive options | Radios or a segmented control, all visible |
| Independent options, any number | Checkboxes |
| About 5–15 options, one choice, tight space | Select |
| 15 or more | Combobox with search |

Put the control in the same group as the thing it changes, or on that group's edge. Two unrelated groups need their own spacing or heading. Use `fieldset` and `legend` for a real set of fields.

```tsx
// ❌ a select hiding two brands, away from the pair it filters
<select aria-label="Brand">
  <option>Levi&apos;s</option>
  <option>Carhartt</option>
</select>

// ✅ both brands visible, labeled with the catalogue they filter
<fieldset>
  <legend className="text-sm font-medium text-indigo-950">Brand</legend>
  <div className="mt-2 flex gap-2">
    <label className="text-sm"><input type="radio" name="brand" /> Levi&apos;s</label>
    <label className="text-sm"><input type="radio" name="brand" /> Carhartt</label>
  </div>
</fieldset>
```
